Near miss for procedure_declaration_syntax: a bare `PROCEDURE Name;`
without `(` is not provably a declaration attempt, so this rule must NOT
fire. The statement still does not parse and unexpected_token reports it
(diag.procedure_declaration_syntax second bullet).
-- input.ssl --
PROCEDURE CalcDiscount;
:RETURN .T.;
-- format --
PROCEDURE CalcDiscount;

:RETURN .T.;
-- diagnostics --
1:11-1:23 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'CalcDiscount' - expected an operator or ';'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:11-1:23 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'CalcDiscount' - expected an operator or ';'
